NNAAMMEE
     ppnnpp — support for “Plug and Play” (PnP) ISA devices

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppnnpp driver enumerates ISA devices which support “Plug and Play ISA
     Specification” in the system.  It assigns ISA bus resources (interrupt
     line, DMA channel, I/O ports, and memory region) to each device and acti‐
     vates it.

     If it cannot assign necessary resources to a PnP ISA device without caus‐
     ing conflict with other devices in the system, the device will not be ac‐
     tivated and will be unavailable to programs.

